    "body": "### Describe the feature or problem you\u2019d like to solve\n\n`gh extension upgrade` should allow flexibility when dealing with prerelease extensions, both by allowing an upgrade directly to the latest prerelease, and by supporting a `--pin` flag.\n\nCurrently:\n\n```shellsession\n$ gh extension upgrade ext\n[ext]: already up to date\n\u2713 Successfully checked extension upgrades\n\n$ gh extension upgrade ext --pin v1.0.0.beta.2\nunknown flag: --pin\n\nUsage:  gh extension upgrade {<name> | --all} [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  --all       Upgrade all extensions\n  --dry-run   Only display upgrades\n  --force     Force upgrade extension\n```\n\n### Proposed solution\n\n* add a `--latest-prerelease` flag that lets the version be drawn from prereleases as well, sorting by version order\n* add a `--to <ver>` flag that will accept any version, prerelease or otherwise\n\nThat'll mean that we don't need to fully release an extension to GA in order to test it.\n\n### Additional context\n\nAdd any other context like screenshots or mockups are helpful, if applicable.\n",
